# Claude Code harness — local-only state. These were previously ignored ONLY via this
# machine's .git/info/exclude and ~/.config/git/ignore, so on a fresh clone a
# harness-created worktree showed up in `git status`. The committed parts of .claude/
# (hooks, skills, settings.json, COORDINATION.md) are deliberately tracked.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Local scratch output — reports, generated PDFs, session notes. Never a build input and never
# something the repo should carry: what lands here is whatever a session happened to write, which
# on this machine included a personal document. Untracked was doing the work by accident; this
# makes it deliberate.
/output/
